    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">20 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Linked list - fast/slow gap</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/remove-nth-node-from-end-of-list/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 19</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Remove Nth Node From End of List</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">You cannot count backwards in a singly linked list, so make the distance do the counting: send one pointer n nodes ahead, then move both until the leader hits the last node. The follower is then parked just before the node to delete. A dummy head makes \"delete the head\" an ordinary case. O(L) time, O(1) space.</p>\n"
